      "worked": "By the chain rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}g'(x)&=f'(-x)\\cdot(-1)\\\\g'(x)&=-f'(-x)<0.\\end{align*}$$\nFor every $x$ in the domain of $g$, the value $-x$ is in the domain of $f$, so $f'(-x)>0$.",
